# Plan: AIS DATA SOURCE Toggle on Global Page

## Context
The user wants a manual two-option toggle (REAL-TIME / DEMO) for the AIS data source on the Global (Globe) page. Currently, the system auto-falls back from real-time AISStream data to demo data when the backend is unavailable. The new toggle must give the user explicit control with no automatic switching.

## Files to Modify

| # | File | Change |
|---|------|--------|
| 1 | `src/lib/store/use-app-store.ts` | Add `aisSource` state + `setAisSource` action |
| 2 | `src/components/globe/ais-source-toggle.tsx` | **New file** — the toggle component |
| 3 | `src/components/map/globe-map-view.tsx` | Remove auto-fallback to demo data |
| 4 | `src/app/page.tsx` | Wire toggle into page, pass correct data, update status indicators |

## Implementation Steps

### Step 1: Zustand Store (`use-app-store.ts`)
- Add `aisSource: "realtime" | "demo"` to `AppState` interface
- Add `setAisSource: (source: "realtime" | "demo") => void` action
- Default value: `"demo"` (safe default — shows demo data on first load)

### Step 2: New Component (`ais-source-toggle.tsx`)
Create `src/components/globe/ais-source-toggle.tsx`:
- Small glass-panel widget matching the existing panel aesthetic
- Two toggle buttons: `[ REAL-TIME ]` and `[ DEMO ]`
- Status indicator: green dot + "REAL-TIME" when realtime selected, amber dot + "DEMO / SIMULATED" when demo selected
- Shows "AISSTREAM" label as the source name
- Props: `aisSource`, `onSourceChange`
- Styled to match existing `LayersPanel` / `DataSourcesPanel` glass-panel aesthetic
- Compact — sits in the left panel stack without dominating the globe

### Step 3: GlobeMapView (`globe-map-view.tsx`)
- Change `effectiveVesselGeoJSON` memo: accept a new prop `dataSource?: "realtime" | "demo"`
- When `dataSource === "realtime"`: use `vesselGeoJSON` prop only, never fall back to `REALTIME_AIS_GEOJSON`
- When `dataSource === "demo"`: always use `REALTIME_AIS_GEOJSON`, ignore `vesselGeoJSON` prop
- Add `dataSource` to `GlobeMapViewProps`

### Step 4: Globe Page (`page.tsx`)
- Import `AisSourceToggle` and `useAppStore` (already imported)
- Read `aisSource` from store
- Compute `effectiveVesselGeoJSON` based on source:
  - `"realtime"` → pass `vesselGeoJSON` from `useAISStream()` (or `null` if unavailable)
  - `"demo"` → pass `REALTIME_AIS_GEOJSON`
- Add `<AisSourceToggle>` to the left panel stack (below `LayersPanel`, above `DataSourcesPanel`)
- Update `dataSources` AIS entry status to reflect actual state:
  - If realtime + connected → `"LIVE"`
  - If realtime + disconnected → `"UNAVAILABLE"`
  - If demo → `"DEMO"`
- Update `statusCards` AIS entry similarly
- Pass `dataSource` prop to `<GlobeMapView>`

## What NOT to Modify
- Monitor, Investigation, SAR, oil detection, environmental functionality — all untouched
- Backend API — no changes
- AIS stream hook internals — works as-is, just conditionally consumed
- Vessel rendering pipeline — same `addVesselLayer()` for both sources
- Other pages — only Global page (`src/app/page.tsx`)

## Verification
- `npm run build` (or `next build`) to verify no type errors
- Visual check: toggle appears in left panel stack on globe page
- REAL-TIME selected: green indicator, attempts AISStream connection, shows "UNAVAILABLE" if backend not running
- DEMO selected: amber indicator, shows 20 preloaded vessels, labeled "DEMO / SIMULATED"
- Switching between modes immediately updates the globe without page refresh
